an lean of roughly eleven points toward the GOP. The 2028 race is an open contest with no incumbent on the ballot, and no candidate-specific fundraising, polling, or expert ratings exist yet for the state. Recent headlines focus on the national primary contests in both parties rather than on Mississippi's general-election picture.\n\nWith no state polls or market pricing to weigh, the forecast rests on fundamentals alone. The state's durable Republican lean points to a GOP win in the low double digits, though the absence of direct polling keeps uncertainty wide. A Democrat would need a national wave well beyond anything currently indicated to put Mississippi in play.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1069, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1631, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1578, "margin": -11.0}]}